WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.070
Speaker 1: Hey.

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.070
So some of you might find this interesting.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:06.370
I've gotten a handful of emails from from
people saying, David, I was loving those interviews

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.590
of Trumpist candidates that you were doing
over the last few months, but you haven't

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.660
done one for a while.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.660
What's going on?

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.690
Well, it's because they keep canceling on
us.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.450
They something is going on.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.119
And I'll tell you what, I believe it is where
the Trump is.

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:19.859
Candidates, they agree to be on the show.

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:21.269
We schedule it.

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:23.750
It's an hour before the show.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.609
And then they cancel and then they say, oh,
well, who will?

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:28.070
And I'll and I'll tell you what I think is
going on.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.140
So as a reminder, we did a bunch of these
Republican candidate interviews of Republicans

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.050
endorsed by Donald Trump.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.530
We interviewed John Gibbs.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.800
That one was while they got almost half a
million views.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.340
I can't imagine it was particularly good for
the John Gibbs campaign.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.360
We did one with Darleen Swofford.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.450
She's the one who could not or refused to
give a straight answer to the question, who

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.949
is the president of the United States?

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:54.780
And we did some others, and none of them really
went that well for the candidates.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.320
But people ask for more.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.630
And so we had more scheduled, I think four
or five different ones.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:05.140
But something has happened between the time
when they agree and the time when we are ready

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.360
to do the interview.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.280
They say, Yes, I'll do it, we get it on the
schedule.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.680
And invariably a few minutes to an hour to
a couple of hours before the interview, they

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.890
cancel.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.610
Sometimes it's a no call, no show, sometimes
it's, Oh, something came up.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:20.690
Oh, we have a conflict.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.710
All right, well, let's reschedule.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:27.420
Yeah, we'll get back to you about rescheduling,
and then they never do.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.420
And it's quite a list now.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.670
Now, I'm not going to name names because.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:37.470
It's it seems inappropriate to name names
and also of the list of five or so.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.220
Some of them might really have had a conflict.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.659
And I don't want to like pick and single out
the wrong person.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:45.790
But obviously, something is going on.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:50.880
Now, our colleague John, who's been scheduling
these and dealing with the schedulers, thinks

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.390
the explanation is very simple.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:58.570
Oftentimes, either the candidate themselves
or if they have a publicist or a communications

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:03.479
person, they get excited that someone wants
to talk to them and they go, Yeah, I'll do

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:04.479
it.

00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:05.479
That sounds good.

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:10.090
They don't research the show, and then they
go to the channel and they see John Gibbs

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:15.350
making a fool out of himself and half a million
views or Darlene Swap for becoming Mehmed

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:19.960
on Twitter with 100,000 views on a stupid
little Twitter clip that we put together because

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.790
she can't say who the president of the United
States is.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.890
And then they say, I'm going to bail out here.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:27.530
So we're available to chat.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:29.220
I want to learn about their ideas.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.770
I want to learn about the whole thing.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:36.670
And I also think I should mention, like, I
kind of get it in a way, doing this show isn't

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.140
going to help them, you know, to win.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.930
Imagine that you're running in the third district
in Michigan or whatever, right?

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:48.400
To win, you need to convince not just all
voters in that third district of Michigan,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.040
because a lot of them are not going to consider
voting for a lunatic Trumpist.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:58.100
You need to convince the low information voters
in the third district of Michigan.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.950
And they're mostly not in my audience.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:00.950
Right.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.490
I mean, this is a show with a mostly progressive
audience.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.490
Yes.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:08.910
Some center right and right wingers, but most
of them don't live in the third District of

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.920
Michigan or whatever the case may be.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.700
So I get it, like at best doing an interview
on this show.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:20.320
It does nothing bad and gets you a little
bit of attention generally, but it's not the

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.180
people that ultimately are going to put you
in office.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.970
And worst case, it gets Mehmed and it hurts
you.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.990
So I can't say I blame them, but I wanted
to put everybody on notice with peace and

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:31.990
love.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.990
Peace and love.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:35.880
We're doing what we can to get more of these
people on the show.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.310
Most of them just decline.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:43.060
And even the ones that agree, I think we now
have four in a row who just bail.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.060
They just bail.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:44.410
They end up not wanting to do it.

